      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We propose a Bayesian adjustment for the misclassification of a binary exposure variable in a matched case-control study. The method admits a priori knowledge about both the misclassification parameters and the exposure-disease association. The standard Dirichlet prior distribution for a multinomial model is extended to allow separation of prior assertions about the exposure-disease association from assertions about other parameters. The method is applied to a study of occupational risk factors for new-onset adult asthma."},
